ank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T02:52:27-07:00","id":101841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/46335-the-triumphant-return-of-the-lets-talk-food-thread?p=101545#post101545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll take a look and see if it is indeed for sale around here somewhere <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Good luck with the hunt <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T14:32:52-07:00","id":102940,"title":"","content":"One of the greatest experiences in my life as far as food goes was going to a Game Warden Banquet. Basically it was like they deep fried and grilled Noah's Ark. I ate things I didn't know could or should be eaten. All confiscated from poachers and such. Was a blast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T05:47:44-07:00","id":103322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/46335-the-triumphant-return-of-the-lets-talk-food-thread?p=101527#post101527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never tried either Venison, Elk or Mutton, there are not those things around here but I'm willing to try them or buffalo if I get the chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elk is like steak that needs to be cut with a goddamned chainsaw. No idea about Venison or Mutton though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T08:44:59-07:00","id":103413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/46335-the-triumphant-return-of-the-lets-talk-food-thread?p=103322#post103322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elk is like steak that needs to be cut with a goddamned chainsaw. No idea about Venison or Mutton though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cut with some pork fat it makes for damn nice sausage with some stronger flavors though.<br /> <br /> Much the same with venison, and mutton... eh. Not my favourite but it's not a bad tasting meat for the most part.<br /> <br /> The general guideline is that any wild meat is going to be stronger in flavour, a bit gamey, and very lean compared to farmed meats. Stewing them, making them into sausage or any other form of ground meat product and they're good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T13:58:24-07:00","id":103630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/46335-the-triumphant-return-of-the-lets-talk-food-thread?p=103322#post103322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elk is like steak that needs to be cut with a goddamned chainsaw. No idea about Venison or Mutton though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elk/moose needs to be hung at cool storage for about a week to tenderise it just like beef, a rabbit at least 2 days and venison at least 5 days. Wild boar the same 4-5 days.<br /> Most game birds and small mammals require no more than a day or so and if the meat hasn't been bled properly it will have that unappealing 'muddy liver' taste<br /> which way too many people associate (wrongly) as gamey-taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T18:12:06-07:00","id":105264,"title":"","content":"Roast Beef and Mashed potatoes for dinner tonight.<br /> <br /> <br /> This stuff is gonna stick in my teeth for weeks, but damn if it doesn't taste great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T00:47:59-07:00","id":106107,"title":"","content":"I just recently learned how to make chicken tikka masala and basmati rice with turmeric flavoring. Mmm-mmm, good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T22:05:39-07:00","id":123606,"title":"","content":"What are the preferred uses for ciabatta bread? I've just been cutting it thick, putting mustard on it, and eating it, but it seems like it must be intended for some more specific use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T05:32:05-07:00","id":123736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/46335-the-triumphant-return-of-the-lets-talk-food-thread?p=123606#post123606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the preferred uses for ciabatta bread? I've just been cutting it thick, putting mustard on it, and eating it, but it seems like it must be intended for some more specific use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently you use them to make panini, and in Argentina, ciabatta sandwiches with minute steak are a thing. Might be worth looking into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T09:21:46-07:00","id":123814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/46335-the-triumphant-return-of-the-lets-talk-food-thread?p=123606#post123606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the preferred uses for ciabatta bread? I've just been cutting it thick, putting mustard on it, and eating it, but it seems like it must be intended for some more specific use.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original use for Ciabatta is to substitute Those long French wheat breads AKA baguettes.<br /> <br /> Bck in the -80's the Italians were so jealous to French about their better breads that they launched a campaign for &quot;Italian national bread&quot; and Ciabatta was born.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T16:11:23-07:00","id":137316,"title":"","content":"So my parents got a new fridge that dispenses carbonated water. I've been using it to make &quot;home made&quot; pop with some syrup stuff. Still haven't gotten the measurements quite right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T18:39:48-07:00","id":137469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/46335-the-triumphant-return-of-the-lets-talk-food-thread?p=137316#post137316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my parents got a new fridge that dispenses carbonated water. I've been using it to make &quot;home made&quot; pop with some syrup stuff. Still haven't gotten the measurements quite right.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of weird... does it have a co2 tank somewhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T18:47:05-07:00","id":138705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/46335-the-triumphant-return-of-the-lets-talk-food-thread?p=137469#post137469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's kind of weird... does it have a co2 tank somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Uses a Co2 Tank behind the Ice Dispenser. You change it with the push of a button, takes a bit to reload.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mom loves the new fridge. I like it too. Keeps food a lot cooler than our last one did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T17:38:29-07:00","id":199464,"title":"","content":"I dislike macaroni and cheese. This is largely because I dislike cheese. Nevertheless, due to horrible and unpreventable mishaps during the Fourth of July dinner I attended, I got some mac and cheese in my potato salad and discovered that mac and cheese is actually pretty tolerable with mustard. Tonight, I tried to make some mac and cheese with mustard, and let me tell you, if you're going to make something you like, don't hold back. Don't hedge your bets and buy the cheap shit, because I bought one of those individual cups of microwavable Kraft mac n cheese, and that shit is fucking <i>gross</i>. No amount of mustard can save it. Oh my god.<br /> <br /> Now I am driving into town for a fucking pizza or something because I had kind of banked on being able to stomach that cup of rottenness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T01:46:00-07:00","id":199810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/46335-the-triumphant-return-of-the-lets-talk-food-thread?p=199464#post199464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is largely because I dislike cheese.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But it's okay, Jim. I don't like mac and cheese either; just too slimy for what is essentially a cheese-delivery system. And if I just wanted some cheese, I would just eat some cheese.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T07:49:06-07:00","id":200028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/46335-the-triumphant-return-of-the-lets-talk-food-thread?p=199464#post199464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dislike macaroni and cheese. This is largely because I dislike cheese. Nevertheless, due to horrible and unpreventable mishaps during the Fourth of July dinner I attended, I got some mac and cheese in my potato salad and discovered that mac and cheese is actually pretty tolerable with mustard. Tonight, I tried to make some mac and cheese with mustard, and let me tell you, if you're going to make something you like, don't hold back. Don't hedge your bets and buy the cheap shit, because I bought one of those individual cups of microwavable Kraft mac n cheese, and that shit is fucking <i>gross</i>. No amount of mustard can save it. Oh my god.<br /> <br /> Now I am driving into town for a fucking pizza or something because I had kind of banked on being able to stomach that cup of rottenness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely will not touch mac and cheese. I find it disgusting and terrible. HOWEVER... pasta in a cheese sauce? That I will eat and find enjoyable. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T08:19:21-07:00","id":200045,"title":"","content":"See, I'm a macaroni and cheese fan. My grandmother would make a batch from scratch every year for Christmas--she's still around and is doing pretty well for a diabetic octogenarian, but the duty's of the sacred Mac &amp; Cheese has fallen to the next generation--and it's always been one of those things that would disappear fast. It's a simple thing, sure, but it's a comfort food for me.<br /> <br /> If I could swing the recipe in batches that would comfortably feed less than a dozen people, then I'd make it myself regularly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":". 07-17-2014, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T15:05:18-07:00","id":201497,"title":"","content":"My new job has me eating a lot of fast food. I'm really starting to hate that part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T15:58:21-07:00","id":201542,"title":"","content":"Ah, I love Ciabatta bread with Fontina, sort of like a cheese grilled sandwich. Just toasting Ciabatta bread is good too.<br /> <br /> I made a Raspberry Semifreddo with Chambord this July from a recipe from the <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Slushed-Frozen-Boozy-Treats-Coolest/dp/1440532184\" target=\"_blank\">Slushed book</a>. I picked up the Chambord long ago from a Bevmo store since it said it was good to put on ice cream (<i>And I was looking for another fruit liquor for baking/cooking besides the Grand Marnier in the house</i>).<br /> <br /> I've mixed carbonated water with Beligan Lambic before, it's really good.<br /> Looking for some food recipes that use Perry, since I'm a big fan of it. Also growing some cherry tomatoes in the backyard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T19:02:23-07:00","id":201697,"title":"","content":"There is a reason i'm not allowed in the kitchen....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v664/kick-the-kitten/dinner2_zps0512b682.png\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v664/kick-the-kitten/dinner2_zps0512b682.png\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v664/kick-the-kitten/dinner2_zps0512b682.png\" target=\"_blank\"> http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v664/kick-the-kitten/dinner2_zps0512b682.png </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This monster of a mess, is tatertots on the bottom layer(enough to cover the bottom of the pan), a dusting of cheese, then alot of scrambled eggs( i think i used a whole dozen....)12oz of cut up bacon(cooked),then topped with 3 cups of country gravy, and shoved into an oven for like 40 minuets @350 degrees.<br /> <br /> It uh lasts for days cause its so filling..It tastes so good though...This is why i'm fat ;&gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> *Yes my kitchen was a terrible mess that day...I'm not allowed to cook cause I make a HUGE mess and i make things like this...haha<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T06:47:02-07:00","id":203800,"title":"","content":"There's a local company that makes organic free trade mexican chocolate. It's amazing, and they have a booth in Haymarket on Wednesdays. They punch me in the wallet every time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.tazachocolate.com/Tours?gclid=CjwKEAjw9LKeBRDurOugs43jnlgSJACUXqHxrUFQ3uT6HXN7gQYlBKw8HwdjJ86mBIVxpe0tUr3qCRoChkLw_wcB\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.tazachocolate.com/cdn/shop/files/taza_b57c02ae-f7fb-4958-be78-7cf302dd108b.png?v=1789668814\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.tazachocolate.com/Tours?gclid=CjwKEAjw9LKeBRDurOugs43jnlgSJACUXqHxrUFQ3uT6HXN7gQYlBKw8HwdjJ86mBIVxpe0tUr3qCRoChkLw_wcB\" target=\"_blank\"> Factory Store &amp; Tours </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.tazachocolate.com/Tours?gclid=CjwKEAjw9LKeBRDurOugs43jnlgSJACUXqHxrUFQ3uT6HXN7gQYlBKw8HwdjJ86mBIVxpe0tUr3qCRoChkLw_wcB\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.tazachocolate.com/Tours?gclid=CjwKEAjw9LKeBRDurOugs43jnlgSJACUXqHxrUFQ3uT6HXN7gQYlBKw8HwdjJ86mBIVxpe0tUr3qCRoChkLw_wcB </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Experience stone ground organic dark chocolate with true grit! Bold flavor and texture, plus it&rsquo;s Non GMO, Direct Trade, gluten free, dairy free, and vegan. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T08:16:44-07:00","id":208349,"title":"","content":"So I happen to be fond of the food truck scene. Dallas is slowly adopting the format; there's a park about a 10-12 minute walk from my current workplace that pulls up about a half-dozen trucks every lunch break, and a couple days a week the square right across the rail line from here gets two-three.<br /> <br /> So, backstory: there's this foodstuff called arancini di riso. It's a sort of meat-stuffed rice ball, breaded up and fried. Given the Texan tendency to fry anything and everything we can (I'm looking at you, fried butter), you'd imagine this would be more common. But sadly, this is not to be: the local Korean barbecue place has something kind of similar. The state fair itself had fried jambalaya. <br /> <br /> And there's a food truck that serves them, but since nobody knows what they are they're listed as &quot;Fried Risotto Balls.&quot; But they don't have a route that comes near where I live, so it's usually a bit of luck of the draw--or knowing that they're going to be over at the food truck yard on a given day, but that's a bit of a drive--to get them. <br /> <br /> Or, most commonly by far, I make up a batch at home. <br /> <br /> There's a point to all this, and I haven't gotten to it yet.<br /> <br /> There's a thai food truck that's going to be at the nearby square. I haven't had them yet, but they have something called &quot;firecracker balls.&quot; After discussing it with the guy running the truck, he agreed absolutely that it was a sort of thai fusion arancine, but again, nobody understood that and the name didn't have a place on the menu. <br /> <br /> So this afternoon that's on my lunch menu. Report to follow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T08:23:29-07:00","id":208354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/46335-the-triumphant-return-of-the-lets-talk-food-thread?p=208349#post208349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I happen to be fond of the food truck scene. Dallas is slowly adopting the format; there's a park about a 10-12 minute walk from my current workplace that pulls up about a half-dozen trucks every lunch break, and a couple days a week the square right across the rail line from here gets two-three.<br /> <br /> So, backstory: there's this foodstuff called arancini di riso. It's a sort of meat-stuffed rice ball, breaded up and fried. Given the Texan tendency to fry anything and everything we can (I'm looking at you, fried butter), you'd imagine this would be more common. But sadly, this is not to be: the local Korean barbecue place has something kind of similar. The state fair itself had fried jambalaya.<br /> <br /> And there's a food truck that serves them, but since nobody knows what they are they're listed as &quot;Fried Risotto Balls.&quot; But they don't have a route that comes near where I live, so it's usually a bit of luck of the draw--or knowing that they're going to be over at the food truck yard on a given day, but that's a bit of a drive--to get them.<br /> <br /> Or, most commonly by far, I make up a batch at home.<br /> <br /> There's a point to all this, and I haven't gotten to it yet.<br /> <br /> There's a thai food truck that's going to be at the nearby square. I haven't had them yet, but they have something called &quot;firecracker balls.&quot; After discussing it with the guy running the truck, he agreed absolutely that it was a sort of thai fusion arancine, but again, nobody understood that and the name didn't have a place on the menu.<br /> <br /> So this afternoon that's on my lunch menu. Report to follow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never post in this thread, mainly because even reading it makes my tummy rumble, but I cannot wait for that report. Sounds yummy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T12:26:41-07:00","id":208561,"title":"","content":"So!<br /> <br /> According to an Italian woman I knew back in college, you have Neapolitan arancini and Sicilian arancini. I generally favor--and make--Sicilian, while per her definition Neapolitan tend not to have stuffing, just being spare rice or risotto rolled up and fried.<br /> <br /> (I just remembered that Kroger occasionally carries a four cheese arancini in this style in their freezer section, but I've found it underwhelming).<br /> <br /> This latter style seems to be closer to what I was served.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, it was still good! It was clearly a snack, though, and not a meal: the two rice balls were maybe a bit larger than chicken eggs (albeit spherical), with a spicy mayo topping like I've seen on some sushi and a carrot-and-something-I-think-might-have-been-daikon along the side. It was panko-breaded, with a delicious crunch to the outside, and a spicy red-curry heat to the jasmine rice itself that was just propped up against the upper levels of acceptable spice and stayed there. It didn't overpower the hints of basil or lemongrass mixed into the rice, and while I'm not a fan of carrots in general, I found the slaw provided a nice acidic contrast to the fireballs (ignore what I said above--they're fireballs, not firecracker balls) and a little extra texture. <br /> <br /> Not the best I've had, but I'd certainly have it again.<br /> <br /> But like I said, we get two or three food trucks. While I was promised a shaved ice truck (we have a few down here that are pretty damn nice), none showed itself. But there was one styling itself &quot;The Great Australian Meat Pie Company&quot; and that certainly sounded promising.<br /> <br /> I ended up getting a shepherd's pie that pretty much stole the show, with rough-cut mushrooms and savory, tender beef in a rich gravy, sprinkled with melting shredded cheese. On top of the whole thing was a towering, airy crust of puff pastry--it definitely looked a little weird as it sat there--it's a sharp visual contrast to the rich brown gravy and its contents, and was probably put on top moments before serving--but the textural juxtaposition was marvelous. I really wish I could go into as much depth on this as I did on the fireballs, but this was ultimately a bit of a simpler dish. Could have used a bit less salt, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> My lips were still tingling from the fireballs after I had the pie, but I think the latter was the serendipitous find of the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T18:55:42-07:00","id":208958,"title":"","content":"Went to grocery store after work. Wasn't going to cook; wanted to pick up rotisserie chicken from heat lamp. Heat lamp was next to end-of-day, discounted doughnuts. Thought, &quot;Fried chicken + waffles = thing; therefore, would rotisserie chicken + doughnuts = thing?&quot; Conducted experiment. Results disappointing. Not <i>bad</i>, exactly, but flavors clash in a way I can't describe. &quot;Like sour hush puppies&quot; is the best I can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T19:17:44-07:00","id":208963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/46335-the-triumphant-return-of-the-lets-talk-food-thread?p=208958#post208958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Went to grocery store after work. Wasn't going to cook; wanted to pick up rotisserie chicken from heat lamp. Heat lamp was next to end-of-day, discounted doughnuts. Thought, &quot;Fried chicken + waffles = thing; therefore, would rotisserie chicken + doughnuts = thing?&quot; Conducted experiment. Results disappointing. Not <i>bad</i>, exactly, but flavors clash in a way I can't describe. &quot;Like sour hush puppies&quot; is the best I can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd suggest looking at the menu for places that mostly serve donuts to see what would likely go with 'em. Tim Hortons or a Dunkin' donuts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T19:26:01-07:00","id":208968,"title":"","content":"Neither of those are anywhere near me, and anyway, I am not committed to doughnut-based cuisine. It was just a thought I had that justified having doughnuts for dinner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T00:41:46-07:00","id":209177,"title":"","content":"Donuts are always a justifiable dinner. <br /> <br /> *loads shotgun shells filled with salt and 18mm d10s*<br /> <br /> Always. -_- &lt;_&lt; &gt;_&gt; ..... &gt;_-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T16:04:48-07:00","id":209554,"title":"","content":"So this must be what they mean when they call it a &quot;polite society&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T18:35:56-07:00","id":209651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/46335-the-triumphant-return-of-the-lets-talk-food-thread?p=199464#post199464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me tell you, if you're going to make something you like, don't hold back. Don't hedge your bets and buy the cheap shit, because I bought one of those individual cups of microwavable Kraft mac n cheese, and that shit is fucking <i>gross</i>. No amount of mustard can save it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried again with a better grade of material; white cheddar with garlic and herbs. I feel like it is very important to get a very thin and very uniform application of mustard, because messing up that very precise equation either ends up with mac n cheese I don't much like or the flavor of mustard with the chewiness of noodles.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T09:39:03-07:00","id":211326,"title":"","content":"So down the road from where my wife and I live, a ramen place is opening today.<br /> <br /> Of course, like most every American college student, former or otherwise, I'm very familiar with instant ramen. It's still a regular appearance on the menu at our apartment, although I tend to dress it up with poached eggs, spinach, and/or red pepper and chili powder. But I've never had the &quot;real thing,&quot; if you will.<br /> <br /> Tonight, that changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T10:55:44-07:00","id":211429,"title":"","content":"Tonight I will buy a cucumber, a squash, and a box of big ol' mushrooms. I will cut the tubers thick, so thick you can only fit one cut in your mouth at a time. I will dump them in a great big Ziploc and pour Italian dressing all over the chunks, then seal the bag and shake it vigorously. I will take the then-dripping fruits (they are technically fruits, right?) out of the bag, skewer them, and toss them onto a grill.<br /> <br /> I expect to eat the fuck out of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T11:57:49-07:00","id":211518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/46335-the-triumphant-return-of-the-lets-talk-food-thread?p=211429#post211429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tonight I will buy a cucumber, a squash, and a box of big ol' mushrooms. I will cut the tubers thick, so thick you can only fit one cut in your mouth at a time. I will dump them in a great big Ziploc and pour Italian dressing all over the chunks, then seal the bag and shake it vigorously. I will take the then-dripping fruits (they are technically fruits, right?) out of the bag, skewer them, and toss them onto a grill.<br /> <br /> I expect to eat the fuck out of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might wanna let them marinate in the dressing for a while if you really want the flavour to pop. Apart from that I approve fully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T13:13:52-07:00","id":211594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/46335-the-triumphant-return-of-the-lets-talk-food-thread?p=211518#post211518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might wanna let them marinate in the dressing for a while if you really want the flavour to pop. Apart from that I approve fully.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. Sounds yummy. And yeah, with the exception of the mushrooms, they are technically fruits. I tried to sign in as AzraelFruits on accident when I read Jim's post. Twice. Stupid brain.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T12:35:29-07:00","id":212681,"title":"","content":"So the ramen place was really good. The whole thing was apparently a bit hectic--they hadn't expected anywhere near the crowd that they got, so about 6:30 they stopped taking reservations, since they figured they were out of things to prepare--especially the titular noodles.<br /> <br /> My wife and I got the same dish, a bowl of ramen with corn, garlic oil, green onions, a soft-boiled egg, and pork--it should have had a single slice, but supplies being what they were we got some tender, coarsely chopped meat instead--with miso mixed into the broth. It was wonderful, and my wife informed me as we drove off that it put what I did to shame. I had no problem conceding this argument. I normally don't like my eggs anything but scrambled and dry, but here it worked. We're definitely coming back.<br /> <br /> TIL Snickerdoodles go really well with coffee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":". 07-29-2014, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T13:37:59-07:00","id":212730,"title":"","content":"That sounds utterly delicious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T17:28:36-07:00","id":212975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/46335-the-triumphant-return-of-the-lets-talk-food-thread?p=211429#post211429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tonight I will buy a cucumber, a squash, and a box of big ol' mushrooms. I will cut the tubers thick, so thick you can only fit one cut in your mouth at a time. I will dump them in a great big Ziploc and pour Italian dressing all over the chunks, then seal the bag and shake it vigorously. I will take the then-dripping fruits (they are technically fruits, right?) out of the bag, skewer them, and toss them onto a grill.<br /> <br /> I expect to eat the fuck out of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eat that with people, man, because an entire cucumber, an entire squash, an entire box of mushrooms, and an entire green bell pepper (I added a green bell pepper) soaked in Italian dressing is a trick that gets old way before you're done eating all that. I may go barf now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T12:03:52-07:00","id":250974,"title":"","content":"I just enjoyed a magnificent chicken cordon bleu made with <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Gruy\u00e8re and served in a sage lemon butter with a side of asparagus.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T03:58:54-07:00","id":251375,"title":"","content":"That sounds ab-so-lu-te-ly delicious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T06:05:31-07:00","id":255977,"title":"","content":"A winter melon soup with mushroom and some fried mushroom with salted and pepper, and it was delicious. The soup's bland flavor help to counter the fried mushroom spiciness.<br /> <br /> But I should really refrain from eating Buddhism veggie meal, since I almost look like Gautama when he was fasting under the Bodhi tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T06:58:52-07:00","id":256013,"title":"","content":"So, first time I've tried to make a veggie meal, and it seems that it was quite a success. Parmesan and tomato crumble, and on the side briks filled with feta and cheese. Then cider cake for desert.<br /> Friends liked it. I'm feeling rather proud right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T09:49:55-07:00","id":256109,"title":"","content":"I don't post much on these forums, but a thread about cooking, this right here, this is my jam. Roleplaying and cooking.<br /> <br /> This summer I found a simple dish that my family absolutely loves. Rinse and mix together 2 cans of black beans, about a pound of corn kernels, a bunch of chopped green onions, and two or three diced avocados. Toss with some olive oil (not too much) and some white vinegar. Chill, and serve in some nice soft pitas. Literally everyone I've fed this to, loved it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/399-disthanes","name":"disthanes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T04:17:25-07:00","id":260500,"title":"","content":"So today I am making strogonof beef with a side of white rice for my mother. I have already diced the beef and sliced the mushroms. The stock is ready next to the minced onion and all is left to do is, well, mix everything just right to make this delicious dish. Wish me luck!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 09-19-2014, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T05:50:01-07:00","id":260538,"title":"","content":"Good luck, Thorbes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T06:19:38-07:00","id":260571,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Jim!<br /> <br /> It was a success! Well, if I had to point one flaw maybe the beef could have done with a bit more cooking (the flesh I could afford was slightly less tender than desired). Other than that it was delicious and I timed it perfectly so my mother could eat it just done after coming from work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T14:47:49-07:00","id":260973,"title":"","content":"So in my wife's family I seem to be the cooking expert. This isn't to say that nobody else in the family can cook--far from it, in fact--but I am the most able-bodied when visiting her parents, and the most able to track down a recipe and generally have a track record of making food I've never prepared before not suck.<br /> <br /> And that's why a month and change ago, I was informed that I was making a &quot;Spanish Basque Almond Cake&quot; next time we visited for my father-in-law's birthday. No recipe supplied, only a vague description. Everything was up to me.<br /> <br /> After running my head into a keyboard a couple times, trying to get that specific series of words to show up in any order, I finally found something. In retrospect, I don't see a significant difference from the Gateau Basque from France, something that turned up much earlier and more often.<br /> <br /> So, that's a somewhat straightforward cake batter and rum-infused pastry cream recipe, save that instead of baking the cake then putting the cream between layers, half the batter was laid out, then the cream, then the rest of the batter (making sure not to let the cream touch the edges of the pan. Ideally, you have a couple pastry bags to make this work. I...did not. There was quite a bit of finangling to make it work, but finally I had a smooth-ish, completely cake-batter top I could scatter sliced almonds over, and then bake.<br /> <br /> When it was done and cooled, I dusted it with powdered sugar.<br /> <br /> The results were very good indeed! The cream really doesn't continue to exist as an individual layer, but the cake is dense, moist, and sweet, with the almonds providing little flavor but a little welcome crunch in contrast. The outer edge of the crust bakes up a just little firmer, drier, and more crumbly than most cakes I'm familiar with; I've heard the texture described as &quot;toothy&quot;, and I suppose that works well enough.<br /> <br /> It might have been a bit too sweet, all told. Everyone seemed happy with it, but there was just a little room for improvement.<br /> <br /> So over the last weekend, I repeated the experiment for my sunday tabletop group, with some tweaks I picked up from a couple other recipes. First was tossing some fresh-grazed orange zest into the batter early on to give it a slightly more distinct flavor. While this made the initial creamed butter, sugar, and vanilla taste more like a dreamsicle, it mellowed out a bit as more ingredients were added.<br /> <br /> Second was more intensive. AFAIK, it's a fairly common shortcut to making jam from berries that amounts to <br /> <br /> equal proportions berries and sugar in separate bowls + time in oven + stir = jam!<br /> <br /> Raspberries were the leading contender, providing a much-needed splash of color, and tartness to contrast with the sweetness of the cake itself.<br /> <br /> Equal proportions sugar and berries ended up being far, far too sweet. Adding lemon to try to rein in the sugar ended up being a bit too pronounced.<br /> <br /> Never being one to admit defeat (or just being too damn stubborn, if you ask my wife), I strained out the pulp and seeds, set this aside, consulted the internet, then heated up the same proportion of raspberries again, stirring it as it rapidly broke down, adding this to the original without any more sugar.<br /> <br /> Now <i>this </i>was tart and in-your-face raspberry. And straining it out a second time, to remove any trace of solid pulp or seed, I simmered it for a while to thicken up, until I had a gorgeous ruby glaze that I was able to spread across the cake after it chilled. It was gorgeous. It was beautiful.<br /> <br /> And despite the fact that we had less than 50% turnout for the game, and one of the people there who did turn up is deathly allergic to berries, the cake lasted only a hair over 24 hours.<br /> <br /> Yep. It's a keeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T03:02:07-07:00","id":261175,"title":"","content":"I love cooking, but the best part for me is definitely the cakes and pastries. Thing is, I like making them more than eating. That's great for my sugar levels I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T22:13:15-07:00","id":261823,"title":"","content":"Made a pot of slow cooked pork and sausage sauce. Quite delicious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T03:41:23-07:00","id":262746,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm food thread <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm an able cook, but when it comes to food I'm all for the eating and not so much for the cooking eheheh I'll leave here just a quick recipe of a dish that amazes me how something so trivial and simple can be so delicious:<br /> <br /> Grab eight Chicken Legs (my favourite but substitute by any other chicken parts you love), drop a pack of Onion Soup (those you just add water to cook) and cover the chicken in beer (usually 2 bottles do the trick), put it in high temperature until it boils then turn it down to the minimum and let it cook in soft fire until the chicken is well done and the sauce a lil bit thick. Serve with white rice and bread for the sauce which is amazing. <br /> <br /> Alternatives are changing the beer for stout or the Onion Soup for Ox Tail Soup.<br /> <br /> P.S. - you can always add spices, but even just like that is great and the best lazy dish I've ever had eheh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T09:33:17-07:00","id":266217,"title":"","content":"Going to the Texas State Fair Monday. Hope to have a thorough report on fried foods for you all when I return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T12:48:20-07:00","id":266371,"title":"","content":"Heh, State Fair food. Its probably unhealthier than half the fast food I'll eat all year, but its why I go there these days.<br /> <br /> <br /> Kinda wish my own visit to the State Fair hadn't gone so utterly pearshaped, probably would've enjoyed the food a tad more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T17:56:33-07:00","id":274328,"title":"","content":"Right, so I should have had this up a week ago.<br /> <br /> While I'd love to have a more complete review here, two problems reared their head:<br /> <br /> 1.) My wife and I met my sister on the way to the fair at a noodle stand in the nearby neighborhood of Deep Ellum. Have I sung the praises of Monkey King Noodle Company? It's a thing of beauty to watch them pull the noodles in the window and toss them in to cook. There's a certain artlessness to them--they've improved in the year or so they've been open, but even now there's some unevenness in the width. I could talk about the wonder that is their spicy beef noodle soup, with fall-apart tender beef and a lingering flavorful heat from the chili oil they sprinkle in.<br /> <br /> I could talk about their wonderful soup dumplings full of savory broth, that need to be handled with care before you bite in, lest the contents spill out.<br /> <br /> And were I to go into detail, my wife assures me I would be remiss if I didn't also speak well of their wonton soup.<br /> <br /> But I'm not hear to talk about that, and odds are good that I've already mentioned them before. I'm talking about the State Fair food. This is only relevant in that we stopped here for lunch, and frankly had more of that than we should have: I approached the fairgrounds with a very full stomach.<br /> <br /> 2.) My wife can certainly approve of good fried food, but her tolerance for it is lower than mine. So whereas we were maybe going to explore three or four of the newest options...well, more on that in a second.<br /> <br /> When we first set out to do this, I said, &quot;Honey, we're here to try new things. You know the fried s'more is good. I know it's good. Let's put that at the bottom of the list so we have room to try new things.&quot;<br /> <br /> ...So of course once we were in range of one of the stands selling them, they were the first thing tickets got spent on. u_u;<br /> <br /> Don't lament, mind. I gave her some grief over this (Disclaimer: She got to review this before I posted), but I can wholly appreciate what we had. The fried s'more is a thing of such wonder and sweetness that I apparently can't quite do it justice in my memory--I only remember just <i>how</i> good it is when it's in my mouth. My wife is a bigger fan than I am; she actually sagged her shoulders and looked like a miserable kitten when someone said they just weren't that impressed with it. But it's still GOOD. It's the molten chocolate, sticky-sweet marshmallow cream, and while the graham cracker doesn't retain its crispiness, its flavor remains in a fried-up beignet dusted with powdered sugar and drizzled with chocolate syrup.<br /> <br /> A while later, after a lot of walking, my wife advising that she was hungry, but really only had space for one more thing. And with that, we decided, we were going to go for the Deep-Fried Texas Bluebonnet. A fried blueberry biscuit stuffed with cream cheese, and topped with whipped cream, blueberries, and white chocolate chips. This...was disappointing. Bad? No. But for the cream cheese in there, it wasn't very rich. If I got a chip or two in there, it was infinitely improved, but all in all, while it'll probably be at the fair next year, there's no way that we'll have it again.<br /> <br /> Far be it from me to let things end on a down note, though. At the next-door stand, they had last year's winner for best flavor, the Fried Cuban Roll. And I literally had JUST enough tickets left to buy one. Now, while the fried bluebonnet <a href=\"http://content-img.newsinc.com/jpg/1304/26527996/14785549.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">LOOKS delicious</a>, the cuban roll is kind of butt-ugly. It looks like an oversized eggroll, and even inside (the outer roll is actually softer and breadier than it initially looks) it's a mass of meat and spices. And the mojo sauce they serve in a cheap plastic cup is also kind of an unappealing shade of green.<br /> <br /> Under other circumstances, I might have given it a pass, but a.) I like cuban sandwiches, and b.) I'd had it last year.<br /> <br /> And it's a good thing; the cuban roll is savory, the chunks of pork tender and flavorful, and the mojo sauce to dip it in adds a welcome, mildly sharp contrast to the whole thing to give it a touch of complexity.<br /> <br /> The only real downside is that splitting it evenly between the two of us, I just wish I'd gotten a little more.<br /> <br /> That's it for this year: only one new menu item tried. Hopefuly next year we'll see some better options, and maybe hit a couple of the things we missed...<br /> <br /> And maybe actually hold off on the fried s'more until later on. But I can't rely on miracles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T07:10:07-07:00","id":278108,"title":"","content":"Time to drink some blood again. We have that local dish which is basically boiled blood mixed with some fat and extra ingredients for flavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T05:11:45-07:00","id":286564,"title":"","content":"anyone got any ideas for some SUPER easy to make and SUPER cheap meals that are not ramen or mac and cheese? Lol <br /> <br /> only thing it CANNOT have is high milk content or high egg content..a bit of cheese is fine though....oh and no vegetables(Except tomatoe and cooked spinach) cause ew <br /> <br /> I need some ideas in hopes something sparks my desire to eat again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum