cavenge much, since her and dad are on this diet of delivered food and haven't been shopping lately.<br /> <br /> Somedays I worry that woman glances at my posts here. Nice of her though. Gonna need to this bacon out of dad's sight, god knows he doesn't need to see me eating it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T20:19:37-08:00","id":414798,"title":"","content":"Okay, so a fly drowned in my Tequila. I took the poor little begger out and put him on a letter near the computer.<br /> <br /> Few minutes later there's a fly zipping all over the place and the one on my letter is missing. I shall call him L\u00e1zaro.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 02-22-2015, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T18:10:15-08:00","id":420935,"title":"","content":"mmmm making a shopping list for next month alll i want right now is spicy foods, so i've deemed march to be the month i shall live to regret! (I am suffering already from painful heartburn that wont go away and have clearly decided i want to turn it up to 1000 cause why the fuck not!)<br /> <br /> I'm thinking spicy fajitas, super spicy chicken enchaldas(i dont like beef or pork all that much so chicken is my go to meat), and various otehr spicy foods for dinner. <br /> <br /> and not spicy stuff for the other meals...cause i dont have a death wish... I want spicy foods so badly, normally i'm not abig fan of spicy either, but right now I'm on a &quot;make it even spicyer/hotter&quot; kick. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T18:37:49-07:00","id":480990,"title":"","content":"I am seriously considering spending 30 bucks on 6 boxes of a limited edition hamburger helper that the outlet store is just about out of but I cant seem to get enough of.... for the record it costs A DOLLAR per box at the outlet store and on payday i intend to clear out whatever they fucking have left ;&gt;&gt; (If it wasnt in an outlet store hamburger helpers around here tend to run about 1.50ish a box)<br /> <br /> Its amazing. Hamburger helper supremes, Cheesy fiesta Nacho....I hate ground beef lately, so i switched it for cut up chicken breast *Drools* Totalllllly worth the PAINFUL heartburn it causes me cause of how spicy it is. (I'm a wimp when it comes to spicy foods lol)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T00:18:52-07:00","id":491433,"title":"","content":"As large midwestern grocery stores go, I have a pretty high opinion of SuperOne, this is because you can buy a pound of salami and a loaf of bread and feed a small army for the next few days.<br /> <br /> Probably healthier than the shit I usually eat at Wal*Mart's deli or whatever fast food joint I and my coworkers drag ourselves into. Word of advice, if anybody ever tries to convince you to go into inventory especially RGIS, slap them. Slap the shit out of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T17:00:11-07:00","id":499502,"title":"","content":"I've been watching a lot of food network since we got cable and i'm starting to enjoy cooking, and not boxed foods lol though i still make a ton of those cause fuck all i'm 8 months pregnant i aint cooking homemade crap every night.<br /> <br /> I'm wanting to make homemade tortilla shells and chips to use with our tacos but i dont even know where to start! Also want to make my own noodles! Anyone got any tried and true recipies send em my way, google is good but i trust word of mouth over internet searches ;&gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> I recently found an AMAZING dough recipie for cinnamon rolls, that with small modification (Replacing the sweet seasoning with garlic or parmesan) makes a beautiful garlic bread, or pizza dough! I'm a happy camper right now.<br /> <br /> I want to try my hand at making a cake from scratch (I have an awesome frosting recipie from scratch that I use on boxed cakes and it tastes great but u've never made a cake on my own that wasnt out of a box) but dear god it sounds like so much work <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T17:56:12-07:00","id":499561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/46335-the-triumphant-return-of-the-lets-talk-food-thread?p=499502#post499502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but u've never made a cake on my own that wasnt out of a box) but dear god it sounds like so much work <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Magic Ratio: 1 part flour, 1 part sugar, 1 part cocoa. Add in a bit of baking powder. Add oil, milk/water, butter and egg to make it into a batter. The more oil and less water the more moist the cake.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/food-network-kitchens/basic-chocolate-cake-recipe.html\" target=\"_blank\">This </a>is a slightly more advanced version, but you'll find the core is still there. <br /> <br /> The pre-mixed packages are pretty much just powdered versions of stuff such as egg and milk mixed in with the basic ingredients, this goes for stuff like hamburger helper as well.<br /> <br /> One of the more economical things you can do is grab some of the components from the bulk goods isle and use 'em instead of the pre-packaged stuff. Also makes it easier to tweak things a bit, mix a little of this into a little of that and the meals don't taste quite the same every time. Also can help cut back on salt.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T14:09:03-07:00","id":506064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/46335-the-triumphant-return-of-the-lets-talk-food-thread?p=499561#post499561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magic Ratio: 1 part flour, 1 part sugar, 1 part cocoa. Add in a bit of baking powder. Add oil, milk/water, butter and egg to make it into a batter. The more oil and less water the more moist the cake.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/food-network-kitchens/basic-chocolate-cake-recipe.html\" target=\"_blank\">This </a>is a slightly more advanced version, but you'll find the core is still there.<br /> <br /> The pre-mixed packages are pretty much just powdered versions of stuff such as egg and milk mixed in with the basic ingredients, this goes for stuff like hamburger helper as well.<br /> <br /> One of the more economical things you can do is grab some of the components from the bulk goods isle and use 'em instead of the pre-packaged stuff. Also makes it easier to tweak things a bit, mix a little of this into a little of that and the meals don't taste quite the same every time. Also can help cut back on salt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ooo i'll have to try that, cause I lvoe the bulk foods section and making stuff ahead of time and making it myself ends up being cheaper then the prepackaged crap.<br /> <br /> i'm super excited I finally perfected my pizza crust recipie!!! Its perfect, and we have a homemade pizza sauce that we also finally got right last night after multiple tries to find the right balance of ingredients to fit the taste we were looking for. Not bragging but i prefer my homemade pizza now over take out hehe (its also a buttload cheaper!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T21:37:49-07:00","id":509569,"title":"","content":"Lemon Mascarpone Trifle. It's delicious, fancy looking, yet so easy to make! Once you find the Mascarpone at least...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2046-rmmstnr","name":"rmmstnr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T02:11:06-07:00","id":957476,"title":"","content":"So, a few weeks ago, I had given myself a pretty awful stomach and hunted up some Baking Soda related curatives for it. I settled on one that was a teaspoon of Vinegar, a teaspoon of baking soda, a table spoon of honey and some hot water.<br /> <br /> It tastes good. Way better than it has any business tasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T09:23:22-07:00","id":957656,"title":"","content":"I've had the maddest craving for halupki recently. They were a specialty of my great grandmother and I realized that I don't think I've actually had them since she passed away. I have her recipe, if not her well honed skill at executing it, so I think I may make my first attempt to do it justice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T09:31:35-07:00","id":957661,"title":"","content":"I like Jappanese Mochi.<br /> <br /> Sesame or peanut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagize